{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32998-b-s-coil-of-blood-souls","id":32998,"title":"B&S: Coil of Blood & Souls","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-19T00:37:26-08:00","id":32998,"title":"B&S: Coil of Blood & Souls","content":"While I am liking the new coils, I do miss the coils involving lasting longer without blood and lasting on animal blood. They gave the Ordo Dracul such a unique flavor as they could spend more time studying than hunting, though indeed they still needed to hunt. I know that blood hunger is a big theme in the game but it's not like we run a feeding scene each session anyhow. I understand that the latter two parts of Coil of Souls aren't very valuable anymore due to their focus on derangements but I did like the first one. Not sure if it could be expanded to create an entire coil, though. Blood, on the other hand, probably could.<br /> <br /> Has anyone put some thought into updating Coil of Blood? What sort of scales could be in place? Or whether the first dot of Souls could be expanded or attached to a different path? Hmm, one could probably add to Souls the reverse of the Red Surrender, quashing the Beast in favour of the Man.<br /> <br /> Ooh, and while I'm at it, what about the Coils of the Ladder and Coils of the Locusts? Do you guys think that still has a place? And if so, what would it look like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T01:08:03-08:00","id":33004,"title":"","content":"I posted this on the old forum in response to Coil of Blood requests, and in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1748-blood-and-smoke-bloodline-disciplines-conversions\">B&amp;S conversion thread</a>, but this seems an appropriate place as well. It's just an outline, but has everything needed to be playable (rules wise).<br /> <br /> <u><b>Coil of the Ascetic</b></u><br /> <b>Dot 1</b>: The Vampire can consume mortal food without need for the blush of life. Consuming enough food provides a bonus to the next Hunger Frenzy roll.<br /> <b>Dot 2</b>: By consuming mortal food the vampire can resolve the Wanton Condition. The Dragon can use mortal eating habits as a touchstone<br /> <b>Dot 3</b>: The Dragon can 'binge' himself over the normal Vitae limits by up to [Coil Dots] Vitae. So long as he is above his normal maximum he needs only spend 1 Vitae to wake every [Coil Dots] days.<br /> <b>Dot 4</b>: The Dragon may continue to take sustenance from Animals and Humans, however he has to deal [BP-2] damage for each Vitae from an animal, or [BP-5] for every point from a human (minimum 1 damage in either case)<br /> <b>Dot 5</b>: The Dragon can eat recently dead flesh (within the last 24 hours) and gain Vitae, the Vitae gained is equal to the Size of the creature. This follows the same restrictions as normal feeding, i.e. if the Vampire is BP 4 a Size 4 animal only gives 2 Vitae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T01:27:29-08:00","id":33009,"title":"","content":"@ PenDragon<br /> <br /> You may wish to revise the dot 4 power. On p. 89 of Blood and Smoke, it says that a vampire may consume blood that is normally denied to it based upon it's blood potency. It must spend a point of willpower per point of vitae it consumes. This means that any vampire can continue to feed despite high BP (though their feeding rate would be then be limited by the rate it regains willpower points). This means that your dot 4 power is only useful if the vampire wants to conserve willpower points, not be the only effective means of feeding without feeding on kindred (and suffering the risks).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T02:10:14-08:00","id":33018,"title":"","content":"I like it, though I might remove 4's damage or reduce it. Any idea what scale abilities could go with it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T02:37:20-08:00","id":33024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DivineWrath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32998-b-s-coil-of-blood-souls?p=33009#post33009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@ PenDragon<br /> <br /> You may wish to revise the dot 4 power. On p. 89 of Blood and Smoke, it says that a vampire may consume blood that is normally denied to it based upon it's blood potency. It must spend a point of willpower per point of vitae it consumes. This means that any vampire can continue to feed despite high BP (though their feeding rate would be then be limited by the rate it regains willpower points). This means that your dot 4 power is only useful if the vampire wants to conserve willpower points, not be the only effective means of feeding without feeding on kindred (and suffering the risks).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, good point. Better point, it's a bookkeeping nightmare. <br /> <br /> I think it can safely be changed to &quot;The Dragon can feed on as though her Blood Potency was [Coil Dots] lower, but doing so requires him to deal twice the damage per Vitae&quot;. Same general effect, vastly less math.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T00:53:12-08:00","id":36812,"title":"","content":"Aww, no one has any thoughts on Scales for that Coil of the Blood?<br /> <br /> No idea about Scales, but I have come up with a Coil of the Ladder and Coil of the Locust option.<br /> <br /> Coil of the Locust<br /> <br /> Enliven the Face (Humanity 5): The kindred\u2019s Humanity doesn\u2019t provide penalties to their interactions.<br /> <br /> Planned Emergence (Humanity 4): The kindred may set a trigger to automatically wake up from torpor.<br /> <br /> Quiet the Soul (Humanity 3): The kindred may spend a Willpower point to ignore a bane taken to ignore a sin. This doesn\u2019t affect banes which affect all kindred.<br /> <br /> Marrow of the Spirit (Humanity 2): The kindred\u2019s Aura changes to match that of a diablerized mortal victim and they gain a 9-Aged against relations of that victim. This lasts only for so long as the soul remains within the kindred (which is for nights equal to Blood Potency).<br /> <br /> Echo of the Soul (Humanity 1): The kindred may recall knowledge known by a diablerized mortal victim using an Intelligence + Academics roll for so long as the soul remains within the kindred (which is for nights equal to Blood Potency).<br /> <br /> Coil of Anoushka\u2019s Ladder<br /> <br /> Denial of Morpheus (Humanity 6): All torpor counts as voluntary torpor when considering one\u2019s mental state and feelings.<br /> <br /> Stir the Blood (Humanity 7): The kindred\u2019s Blood Potency is halved to determine the duration of torpor.<br /> <br /> Rise Above Thirst (Humanity 8): The kindred may spend only a single blood to awaken for a week.<br /> <br /> The Open Cage (Humanity 9): The kindred may spend a point of Willpower to automatically resist a frenzy.<br /> <br /> Divorce the Clan (Humanity 10): The kindred doesn\u2019t suffer from sin-based banes, including clan or bloodline weaknesses for so long as they don\u2019t use any disciplines that night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T02:15:28-08:00","id":36840,"title":"","content":"My variant on Coil of the Ascetic, complete with names and a single scale. Hope you don't my tinkering.<br /> <br /> The Coils of the Ascetic (Onyx Path)<br /> Consumption of Inner Peace \u2022<br /> This gluttonous path allows a Kindred to control the flow of Vitae in their body and the Beast\u2019s reaction to such food. At this level the Dragon can accept alien foods (like human foods) and use its weight to confuse the Beast as to whether it is currently sated. Thus not only can the Dragon eat mortal food without using Blush of Life but doing so provides a +2 bonus to their next Hunger Frenzy roll. They need to regurgitate the food at the end of the night.<br /> <br /> Comfort Eating \u2022\u2022<br /> A Dragon no longer takes witnessing a mortal eating food as a sin at Humanity 9 (CHECK THIS). Eating mortal food also allows the Kindred to resolve the Wanton Condition and the player may select mortal eating habits as a Touchstone. Mortal food also tastes bland rather than like ash to the Dragon\u2019s mouth.<br /> <br /> Binge Drinking \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> The Dragon can \u2018binge\u2019 himself over the normal Vitae limits by up to [Coil Dots] Vitae. So long as he is above his normal maximum he needs only spend 1 Vitae to wake every [Coil Dots] days.<br /> <br /> Feeding Below One\u2019s Beast \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> The Dragon may continue to take sustenance from Animals and Humans even after his Blood Potency has risen to the point where he would normally need to eat the next level higher. However he has to drink [BP-2] points (dealing equivalent damage) for each Vitae taken from an animal when his Blood Potency ranges between 3 and 5. Once Blood Potency has reached 6, the Kindred deals [BP-5] for every vitae taken from a human and [BP-10] for every vitae taken from an animal.<br /> <br /> Carrion Feeding \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> The Dragon can eat recently dead flesh (within the last 24 hours) and gain Vitae, the Vitae gained is equal to the Size of the creature. This follows the same restrictions as normal feeding, i.e. if the Vampire is BP 4 a Size 4 animal only gives 2 Vitae. The consumed flesh is vaporised within the Dragon\u2019s belly and its absorption is thus assured. Consuming a human\u2019s corpse is a Humanity 5 sin as cannibalism is quite the breaking point.<br /> <br /> Scales of the Ascetic<br /> Moment of Comprehension<br /> Prerequisite Coil: Comfort Eating<br /> Procedure: TBA.<br /> <br /> Outcome: There\u2019s something primal about humans sharing food and now that you can mildly indulge with them you can take advantage of this. You gain a +2 bonus to Empathy rolls on humans after you have shared a meal together.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T06:07:10-08:00","id":36888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Laraqua</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32998-b-s-coil-of-blood-souls?p=36812#post36812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coil of Anoushka\u2019s Ladder<br /> <br /> Denial of Morpheus (Humanity 6): All torpor counts as voluntary torpor when considering one\u2019s mental state and feelings.<br /> <br /> Stir the Blood (Humanity 7): The kindred\u2019s Blood Potency is halved to determine the duration of torpor.<br /> <br /> Rise Above Thirst (Humanity 8): The kindred may spend only a single blood to awaken for a week.<br /> <br /> The Open Cage (Humanity 9): The kindred may spend a point of Willpower to automatically resist a frenzy.<br /> <br /> Divorce the Clan (Humanity 10): The kindred doesn\u2019t suffer from sin-based banes, including clan or bloodline weaknesses for so long as they don\u2019t use any disciplines that night.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it, but isn't it going to be incredibly hard for a Dragon to go up in Humanity? Also might be weird for a kindred wanting to go up in humanity (so to speak) being part of such a... questionable organization to begin with.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T07:15:09-08:00","id":36906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32998-b-s-coil-of-blood-souls?p=36888#post36888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it, but isn't it going to be incredibly hard for a Dragon to go up in Humanity? Also might be weird for a kindred wanting to go up in humanity (so to speak) being part of such a... questionable organization to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was a little clearer in materials prior to Blood &amp; Smoke, but there is a faction of the Ordo Dracul composed of vampires who are driven to find a way to defeat the Curse not necessarily because they want to become a greater monster, but because they don't want to be a monster and want to minimize the factors driving them to be one. Anoushka's Ladder is a deprecated coil within the Order, viewed by many Dragons as a shortsighted and self-defeating practice, but it is explicitly followed by vampires who seek divine forgiveness, spiritual purity, absolution, or whatever you want to call the way out of the Curse back to mortality.<br /> <br /> <i>Edit: People looking for other alternatives of Coils geared towards escaping monstrocity could take a look at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/34907-before-the-bomb-blood-smoke-tokyo-expanded\">Before the Bomb</a> supplement too. The Noble Paths of the Fugenkai, a nirvana cult written up there, were created using the original three Coils of the Dragon as a base for inspiration, although the Fugenkai is more interested in defeating certain parts of the Curse than others; defeating torpor and enhancing the blush of life, for example, aren't pursued. They are, however, more Humanity-oriented than the Order, generally speaking.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 12-25-2013, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T11:58:10-08:00","id":36981,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Anoushka's Ladder is a set of coils of that does not mesh well with the philosophy of the Ordo Dracul. It is an Apocryphal coil. Such coils don't overcome the curse (like proper coils should), they twist, warp, subvert the curse. Consequentially, they are not philosophically compatible with the normal coils. Getting found out that you know such coils is a good way to get kicked out of the order (and to be rendered ash a few days later). So if the coils look too wierd, too pious, too vile, too whatever, that is kinda the point of the devs making them.<br /> <br /> You can find info on these coils on (Ordo Dracul covenant book, p. 176).<br /> <br /> Where the rest of order thinks that they should defy God, those who pursue this path thinks they can gain forgiveness in the eyes of God (or at least some of them do). Its basically seeking Golconda though the use of coils. Its a difficult path, one they expect to have to walk before get the rewards. They are quite willing to lose their vampiric powers if they think they they can get ride of the curse as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","user":"DivineWrath","date":". 12-25-2013, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T13:36:44-08:00","id":37000,"title":"","content":"That's pretty interesting. I've got a vampire character who was a doctor in life, who's trying to find ways to improve Kindred society with a combination of her old medical/psychological knowledge, and new occult lore. It was hard fitting her into any sort of faction, since any organisation that does research in Kindred-land seems to use inhumane practices. I might have to check these apocryphal coils out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T13:59:37-08:00","id":37005,"title":"","content":"Honestly, she sounds like a Carthian to me, in that case. I know they sound awfully political, but the Night Doctors provide an example of Carthians using the physiology angle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T14:39:46-08:00","id":37024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32998-b-s-coil-of-blood-souls?p=36888#post36888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like it, but isn't it going to be incredibly hard for a Dragon to go up in Humanity? Also might be weird for a kindred wanting to go up in humanity (so to speak) being part of such a... questionable organization to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Requiem, the Dragons had the best potential for retaining humanity:<br /> Blood 1 means you don't have to feed as often.<br /> Blood 2 means you can always feed from animals<br /> <br /> Banes 1&amp;2 allow to be active in the day, to better interact with mortals.<br /> <br /> Beast 1 &amp; 3: shuts down frenzy.<br /> <br /> Soul 1: Humanity no longer acts as a cap for dice pools involving interactions with mortals. This allows for much more healthy interaction with mortals than Dominate, Majesty and Nightmare. (Dominate, Majesty and Nightmare are much better for getting your own way).<br /> <br /> The Dickery of the ordo often seemed gratuitous.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T14:51:04-08:00","id":37031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32998-b-s-coil-of-blood-souls?p=37005#post37005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, she sounds like a Carthian to me, in that case. I know they sound awfully political, but the Night Doctors provide an example of Carthians using the physiology angle.</div> </div> </div> </div>She's sorta going that angle already. She'd be in the Carthians by now if a whole lot of inter-covenant dickery hadn't caused an awful lot of political upheaval and subsequent chaos. The Night Doctors are really inhumane though, to the point that other Kindred are sort of scared of them. She wouldn't fit in. Not to mention that they're most concerned with developing surgical techniques and ignore the occult angle, which is not what my character is trying to do. She could always start her own sub-group, of course...<br /> <br /> I haven't gotten B&amp;S yet (I'm hoping to purchase the pdf this friday, but paypal is a bit slow around this time of year! Them banks.), so can someone tell me if there's still a explicit ban on being part of two covenants? (past the first status dot, that is) Elsewise trying for a Carthian with Dracul ties (or an Ordo Draco member who is politically active through Carthians) might be a viable long term goal, after a looot of trust gaining on both sides.<br /> <br /> Campaign has been on hiatus while waiting for B&amp;S, so I'm just mainly gathering ideas for character goals right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T14:52:53-08:00","id":37033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32998-b-s-coil-of-blood-souls?p=37031#post37031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't gotten B&amp;S yet (I'm hoping to purchase the pdf this friday, but paypal is a bit slow around this time of year! Them banks.), so can someone tell me if there's still a explicit ban on being part of two covenants? (past the first status dot, that is) Elsewise trying for a Carthian with Dracul ties (or an Ordo Draco member who is politically active through Carthians) might be a viable long term goal, after a looot of trust gaining on both sides.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's explicity allowed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T01:01:54-08:00","id":37221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32998-b-s-coil-of-blood-souls?p=37031#post37031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't gotten B&amp;S yet (I'm hoping to purchase the pdf this friday, but paypal is a bit slow around this time of year! Them banks.), so can someone tell me if there's still a explicit ban on being part of two covenants? (past the first status dot, that is) Elsewise trying for a Carthian with Dracul ties (or an Ordo Draco member who is politically active through Carthians) might be a viable long term goal, after a looot of trust gaining on both sides.</div> </div> </div> </div>The revised status merit is Kindred Status, p. 113 . You can have up to 5 dots of status for covenants, but you must belong to one of them, and no other covenant may have as many dots of status as your primary (for example, 3 dots primary &amp; 2 dots in one other covenant, or 2 dots primary &amp; 1 dot in 3 other covenants). Sharing covenant secrets is still a good way to lose dots and bring a quick end to one's requiem.<br /> <br /> The merit (Right of Return, p. 116) removes Carthian Status dots from the equations when determining your status dots. Its like they don't exist. However, the merit does have some drawbacks, so its not perfect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T06:06:45-08:00","id":37293,"title":"","content":"For Vampires, nothing ever is <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'll look into this when I get the pdf. (hopefully tomorrow!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T12:02:40-08:00","id":42402,"title":"","content":"PenDragon, Laraqua, I really, really like your ideas for a Hunger-related Coil! If you don't mind, here is how I've reworked them together.<br /> <br /> Mystery of the Hunger / Coil of Hunger<br /> <br /> Denial of Want \u25cf<br /> When the Dragon spends vitae to allow her to eat or drink that effect lasts for a full night. In addition, she no longer has to vomit up the meal afterwards. Instead, her vitae acts to break down the meal and adds it to her own substance, effectively digesting it (stuffing her stomach beyond its capacity will make her throw up, though). Eating an amount of food comparable with a normal, human meal provides a +2 bonus to the next Hunger Frenzy roll. The meal must be something nominally edible, though the vampire is immune to any mundane form of food poisoning. Also, if the Dragon ever fails a roll to resist hunger-based Frenzy, spending a Willpower point allows her to re-roll. The Dragon no longer takes witnessing a mortal eating food as a sin at Humanity 9.<br /> If the Dragon makes a habit of consuming mortal meals in at least once per night, she may use this ritual as a Touchstone. Leaving off this ritual for a month or longer while active destroys the Touchstone.<br /> <br /> Mortal Banquet \u25cf\u25cf<br /> Eating and digesting food does no longer requires the Blush of Life. By consuming a human meal the vampire can resolve the Wanton Condition. Eating a meal made from fresh meat dead within the last 24 hours will also heal one level of bashing or lethal damage, whichever is right-most on the Health track. She may only consume one such meal per three hours.<br /> <br /> <br /> Minimize Subsistance \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> As the Dragon masters her Hunger, she learns to taper off her reliance on vitae. Each vitae spent waking up allows the Dragon to rise a number of consecutive nights equal to her rating in the Coil of Hunger. Furthermore, eating a meal suitable for healing that includes at least 1kg of flesh restores 1 vitae, as long as the flesh comes from a creature whose vitae can substain the Dragon.<br /> <br /> Potency of Vitae \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> At this level the Dragon has learned to regulate the concentration of the vitae itself. Treat the Dragon\u2019s Blood Potency as three lower when determining the kind of vitae she can subsist on without spending Willpower (animal, human or supernatural) and increase the size of her Blood Pool by her rating in the Coil of Hunger.<br /> <br /> The Ascetic\u2019s Diet \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> At the pinnacle of the Mystery of the Hunger, the Dragon can survive on even the thinnest of blood and resist the lure of even the richest. Regardless of her Blood Potency the Dragon can subsist on any kind of blood, be it animal, human or supernatural, without spending Willpower. Furthermore, the Dragon halves the quantity of cold human blood needed to constitute one vitae if her BP is greater than 1 and also gains more vitae than usual from animals (Size 2-3 animals provide 4 Vitae each, Size 4-5 animals provide 6; each point of Size above that adds 2 more Vitae available). If the Dragon does imbibe Kindred vitae, she has a +5 bonus to resist Vitae Addiction; this bonus also applies to resist the side effects of drinking the blood of any other supernatural being and the Resolve+Composure roll to resist the opportunity to drink Vitae if she\u2019s already addicted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","name":"Ophion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T19:29:58-08:00","id":42639,"title":"","content":"I'm concerned that last dot makes Dragons too powerful, because it essentially negates the chief reason for Vampires to go into Torpor, and also negates half the bonus of the previous dot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T00:03:53-08:00","id":42738,"title":"","content":"What do you means, &quot;negates&quot;? It improves it's prerequisite! With Potency of Vitae a vampire who was able to feed only on people can drink animal blood again and a vampire with high BP (but not <i>too</i> high) can feed on humans again, with The Ascetic\u2019s Diet everybody can feed on animals. You don't say that Vigor 2 negates Vigor 1 because it does the same thing, only better, surely?<br /> <br /> Regarding the fact that the Mystery makes Torpor a lot less necessary for elders, that's entirely intended and exactly what PenDragon's coil does, what the old Coil of Blood did, and pretty much what Sanguinary Invigoration does up to BP 9.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","name":"Ophion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T00:25:06-08:00","id":42748,"title":"","content":"Mea culpa, you're right on it improving. I think there's something to be said about Sanguinary Invocation being a scale that isn't terribly convenient, and that the old Coil is outdated, and that PenDragon's would have the same issue. I'm a huge fan of the whole thing, I'm just expressing that I'm not sure that it's ideal for that reason. Plus, I kind of like Sanguinary Invocation filling that niche nicely.<br /> <br /> I'll try to think on any alternative ideas for a fifth dot, but failing that, what you've got is pretty top notch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T05:25:14-08:00","id":42822,"title":"","content":"Thanks. The idea is that when the other Covenants and the younger Dragons will start to realize the implications of what this mystery do things will become <i>interesting</i>.<br /> <br /> If you want a version of the fifth coil that makes unlife for the very eldest only marginally more comfortable, so that they will eventually choose to go sleep for a couple of centuries, would this work for you?<br /> <br /> The Ascetic\u2019s Diet \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<br /> The Dragon calculate the quantity of cold human blood needed to constitute one vitae <b>as if her BP were 3 points lower (minimum 1</b>) and also gains more vitae than usual from animals (Size 2-3 animals provide 4 Vitae each, Size 4-5 animals provide 6; each point of Size above that adds 2 more Vitae available).<br /> If the Dragon's Blood Potency is so high that even Potency of Vitae can't help her assimilate mortal blood, the pinnacle of the Coil comes to her rescue: <b>she gains 1 Vitae for every 5 damages she inflicts to a human by feeding as long as her BP is 9; when her BP reaches 10, she needs to inflict 10 levels of damage for 1 vitae. </b>She can also assimilate mortal blood by spending Willpower like the other elders, if she chooses to do so, or try to turn fresh human meat in vitae by eating it, but she needs at least 5 kg of flash (taken from a single &quot;donor&quot;) and is able to do this only once every night ( for the rest of the day, ingesting anything else after this meal will result in vomiting and loss of 1 vitae).<br /> <b>If the Dragon is still able to drink human blood without spending Willpower, by virtue of Potency of Vitae or her naturally low BP, she takes two Vitae for the very first damage she inflicts to her human victims by feeding. If she has already drunk from that particular mortal in the last 24 hours, though, this doesn't happen.</b><br /> If the Dragon imbibes Kindred vitae, she has a +5 bonus to resist Vitae Addiction; this bonus also applies to resist the side effects of drinking the blood of any other supernatural being and the Resolve+Composure roll to resist the opportunity to drink Vitae if she\u2019s already addicted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1866,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","user":"Ophion","date":". 01-05-2014, 08:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","name":"Ophion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T08:35:40-08:00","id":42896,"title":"","content":"I've written up an updated version of the Coil of Blood for use in my game. I incorporated the text from the old coil and added two new levels. I'm also planning a Scale that would allow the dragon to alchemically store blood that could avoid the diminished returns that usually apply to stored blood. Anywho, use it or don't, but this is probably what I will use in my game.<br /> <br /> <b>Coil of Blood</b><br /> Vampires must feed on living blood to survive, and only the weakest of the Kindred can draw sustenance from the blood of animals. The Coil of Blood seeks to lift this requirement, allowing the Kindred to feed on their own terms, rather than forever be slaves to their hunger.<br /> <br /> \u25cf<b>Resistance to Blood\u2019s Hold</b><br /> The Kindred\u2019s path to a greater understanding of the Blood begins by mastering her hunger. The Dragon takes two extra dice to any roll to resist hunger, or to resist frenzy due to hunger or seeing/smelling blood.<br /> <br /> \u25cf\u25cf<b>Blood Seeps Slowly</b><br /> The Dragon\u2019s undead body doesn\u2019t demand as much Vitae to animate itself as do those of other, less enlightened Kindred. The player need spend only one Vitae for his character to wake for a number of nights equal to the vampire\u2019s Resolve. So, a Kindred with a Resolve of 2 loses a Vitae every other night for rising.<br /> <br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<b>Blood of Beasts</b><br /> No matter what the vampire\u2019s Blood Potency is, she can take sustenance from animals and humans.<br /> <br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<b>Empowered Blood</b><br /> When the Kindred burns Vitae to enhance a physical attribute her knowledge of the Blood yields greater results. Attributes enhanced by burning Vitae receive a +4 instead of the usual +2.<br /> <br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<b>Perspicacious Blood</b><br /> The character gains three Vitae for every two Vitae she takes from a human, and receives double the Vitae consumed from Kindred or other supernatural vessels.<br /> <br /> <br /> -Slag","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T10:34:58-08:00","id":42987,"title":"","content":"Well I prefer my version of course but I suppose yours fits better if you're converting an ongoing chronicle. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Just a couple of things:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32998-b-s-coil-of-blood-souls?p=42896#post42896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<b>Empowered Blood</b><br /> When the Kindred burns Vitae to enhance a physical attribute her knowledge of the Blood yields greater results. Attributes enhanced by burning Vitae receive a +4 instead of the usual +2.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm wondering, can a vampire with BP2+ spend more than 1 Vitae to activate Physical Intensity? If so, this could get kinda ridiculous. If not, this is pretty cool and definitely coil material.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32998-b-s-coil-of-blood-souls?p=42896#post42896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<b>Perspicacious Blood</b><br /> The character gains three Vitae for every two Vitae she takes from a human, and receives double the Vitae consumed from Kindred or other supernatural vessels.</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as I like this old power it goes to very weird places. Do you plan to do something about the spontaneous generation of vitae that occurs in Hungarian Marriages (when two vampires with this coil feed from each other) or you're cool with that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","name":"Ophion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T20:17:29-08:00","id":43309,"title":"","content":"I know mathematically that spontaneous vitae generation could theoretically become a problem but I only have one character following this coil. I figure I'd just cross that bridge if I ever got to it (which I don't expect to). As to your other question, I think you can only use Physical Intensity to increase each physical stat once, so you wouldn't be able to add the +2 (or in this case +4) more than once to a given stat.<br /> <br /> -Slag","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T20:39:46-08:00","id":43316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32998-b-s-coil-of-blood-souls?p=43309#post43309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know mathematically that spontaneous vitae generation could theoretically become a problem but I only have one character following this coil. I figure I'd just cross that bridge if I ever got to it (which I don't expect to). As to your other question, I think you can only use Physical Intensity to increase each physical stat once, so you wouldn't be able to add the +2 (or in this case +4) more than once to a given stat.<br /> <br /> -Slag</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, you are able to spend all your vitae per turn on it, or healing wounds. At blood potency 10, this means that a character could add 30 dice to a physical action.<br /> <br /> Mind you these only last for a turn, rather than a scene, and quickly deplete you if your using it all... and you won't have any to heal if necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T13:37:17-08:00","id":43700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32998-b-s-coil-of-blood-souls?p=43309#post43309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know mathematically that spontaneous vitae generation could theoretically become a problem but I only have one character following this coil. I figure I'd just cross that bridge if I ever got to it (which I don't expect to).</div> </div> </div> </div> You only need one vampire and one ghoul.<br /> <br /> 1. Drink 2 points of blood from the ghoul. Gain 3 vitae.<br /> 2. Give the ghoul 2 points of vitae to heal the 2 lethal damage. Net Profit 1 vitae.<br /> 3. Drink 2 points of blood from the ghoul. Gain 3 vitae. Total Vitae 4<br /> 4. Give the ghoul 2 points of vitae to heal the lethal damage. Net Profit 2 vitae.<br /> <br /> Repeat forever.<br /> <br /> You can do the same with 2 vampires even if only one of them has the coil.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T14:00:00-08:00","id":43714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32998-b-s-coil-of-blood-souls?p=42896#post42896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've written up an updated version of the Coil of Blood for use in my game. I incorporated the text from the old coil and added two new levels. I'm also planning a Scale that would allow the dragon to alchemically store blood that could avoid the diminished returns that usually apply to stored blood. Anywho, use it or don't, but this is probably what I will use in my game.<br /> <br /> <b>Coil of Blood</b><br /> Vampires must feed on living blood to survive, and only the weakest of the Kindred can draw sustenance from the blood of animals. The Coil of Blood seeks to lift this requirement, allowing the Kindred to feed on their own terms, rather than forever be slaves to their hunger.<br /> <br /> \u25cf<b>Resistance to Blood\u2019s Hold</b><br /> The Kindred\u2019s path to a greater understanding of the Blood begins by mastering her hunger. The Dragon takes two extra dice to any roll to resist hunger, or to resist frenzy due to hunger or seeing/smelling blood.</div> </div> </div> </div> I consider this very weak, I'd go for full on immunity to hunger frenzy.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32998-b-s-coil-of-blood-souls?p=42896#post42896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u25cf\u25cf<b>Blood Seeps Slowly</b><br /> The Dragon\u2019s undead body doesn\u2019t demand as much Vitae to animate itself as do those of other, less enlightened Kindred. The player need spend only one Vitae for his character to wake for a number of nights equal to the vampire\u2019s Resolve. So, a Kindred with a Resolve of 2 loses a Vitae every other night for rising.</div> </div> </div> </div> Very weak. This basically gives you a number of &quot;free vitae&quot; that can only be used to wake up; even with resolve 10 you will still not have enough &quot;free vitae&quot; to be free from hunting. A coil costs 3 to 4 XP, for that you could buy Herd 3 or 4 which would give you 6 or 8 BP per week, 6 BP is equal to this coil with Resolve 7, Herd at 8 BP is better than any degree of this coil, as you not only pay you cost of living but you get one BP left over. I'd consider something like Resolve + Stamina nights or 1 vitae per week.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32998-b-s-coil-of-blood-souls?p=42896#post42896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<b>Blood of Beasts</b><br /> No matter what the vampire\u2019s Blood Potency is, she can take sustenance from animals and humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great when you get to high blood potency, worthless before BP 3. I'd consider putting it as the 5th dot so it isn't a speedbump for low BP vampires.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32998-b-s-coil-of-blood-souls?p=42896#post42896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<b>Empowered Blood</b><br /> When the Kindred burns Vitae to enhance a physical attribute her knowledge of the Blood yields greater results. Attributes enhanced by burning Vitae receive a +4 instead of the usual +2.</div> </div> </div> </div> Doesn't seem broken, just kind of boring.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32998-b-s-coil-of-blood-souls?p=42896#post42896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<b>Perspicacious Blood</b><br /> The character gains three Vitae for every two Vitae she takes from a human, and receives double the Vitae consumed from Kindred or other supernatural vessels.</div> </div> </div> </div> Infinite Blood generator.<br /> <br /> <br /> Given that feeding on other vampires is a thing, I'd consider putting immunity to the blood bond and blood addiction in there somewehere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T15:21:43-08:00","id":43743,"title":"","content":"NineDaysDead, I like your replacement idea for the 5th dot. I think resistance to Blood Bond would be an excellent repacement. As for the Empowered Blood controversy, I reread Physical Intensity and, while I realize that the text is unclear, I don't think it is intended to be applicable multiple times.<br /> <br /> -Slag","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T04:35:31-08:00","id":44074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32998-b-s-coil-of-blood-souls?p=43743#post43743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">NineDaysDead, I like your replacement idea for the 5th dot. I think resistance to Blood Bond would be an excellent repacement. As for the Empowered Blood controversy, I reread Physical Intensity and, while I realize that the text is unclear, I don't think it is intended to be applicable multiple times.<br /> <br /> -Slag</div> </div> </div> </div>not multiple times, you just put more blood in it all at once.<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/42991-b-s-physical-intensity-and-high-bp?p=43164#post43164\"> Claire confirmed that reading of the rules</a>, and unless Rose goes &quot;wait that's not what I meant at all&quot;...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","name":"Ophion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T15:16:46-08:00","id":45161,"title":"","content":"Very well done, Ophion, Pendragon, and Laraqua. I fancy your work a lot and I'm going to adopt Ophion's version of the Coil and Mystery of Hunger as the B&amp;S replacement for Coil of Blood until and unless an official version is adopted. Frankly I find this a much, much better fit for the third basic Coil of the Dragon than Coil of the Voivode.<br /> <br /> To minimize the need for blood is central to the trans-vampiric Great Work of overcoming the flaws and limitations of the 'Curse' just like to overcome the banes, undead nature, and the Beast. To counter the effects of Blood Potency on feeding looks of great usefulness to all Dragons that expect to become elders. On the contrary, Coil of the Voivode only looks useful to a subset of elders that plan to develop a small army of thralls.<br /> <br /> Slagheap, your more direct conversion has merit, too, but I think the other version fits B&amp;S as a whole somewhat better.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T19:07:12-08:00","id":45292,"title":"","content":"Thanks Irioth, I'm glad you like it! I agree with you about the Coil of the Voivode (very nice scales though) that's why I've tried to make it both useful and appealing to a wide range of different characters: those who just wants to kill as few people as possible, those who think that mastery of the self comes from mastery of wants, those who think that recovering part of what makes humans human is necessary to transcend humanity and vampirism both and those who think that if they have to be a mad doctor feeding on people they may as well be Hannibal Lecter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","name":"Ophion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T12:57:23-08:00","id":45794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32998-b-s-coil-of-blood-souls?p=45161#post45161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very well done, Ophion, Pendragon, and Laraqua. I fancy your work a lot and I'm going to adopt Ophion's version of the Coil and Mystery of Hunger as the B&amp;S replacement for Coil of Blood until and unless an official version is adopted. Frankly I find this a much, much better fit for the third basic Coil of the Dragon than Coil of the Voivode.<br /> <br /> To minimize the need for blood is central to the trans-vampiric Great Work of overcoming the flaws and limitations of the 'Curse' just like to overcome the banes, undead nature, and the Beast. To counter the effects of Blood Potency on feeding looks of great usefulness to all Dragons that expect to become elders. On the contrary, Coil of the Voivode only looks useful to a subset of elders that plan to develop a small army of thralls.<br /> <br /> Slagheap, your more direct conversion has merit, too, but I think the other version fits B&amp;S as a whole somewhat better.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is so much more to the Order than just overcoming banes. Mastering and perfecting existing advantages are just as much part of their philosophy. Voivode shows it most prominently.<br /> <br /> Of course, experimentation and customization are equally important. Coils aren't just a bundle of fancy powers, they are a path to personal transcendence, to become something fundamentally different than you were before. Not every Coil will appeal to every character, because not every character shares the same vision of transcendence. Playing with and adapting Coils to better fit ones personal objectives is not simply possible, but expected and encouraged. Hopefully that can be showcased more in later books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T14:31:38-08:00","id":45851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32998-b-s-coil-of-blood-souls?p=45794#post45794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is so much more to the Order than just overcoming banes. Mastering and perfecting existing advantages are just as much part of their philosophy. Voivode shows it most prominently.<br /> <br /> Of course, experimentation and customization are equally important. Coils aren't just a bundle of fancy powers, they are a path to personal transcendence, to become something fundamentally different than you were before. Not every Coil will appeal to every character, because not every character shares the same vision of transcendence. Playing with and adapting Coils to better fit ones personal objectives is not simply possible, but expected and encouraged. Hopefully that can be showcased more in later books.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is entirely true, and I agree with your point. My own argument was simply that as things stand, feeding limitations look much more like one of the most basic/common/important aspects of vampirism that Dragons would seek to improve first and foremost, much like banes, frenzies, and the corpse-like body, rather than to further enhance the bonding properties of Vitae. Therefore I would really expect Hunger to be one of the most common/basic Coils, and Voivode a relatively obscure secondary Coil, kinda like one that would focus on torpor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 01-09-2014, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T18:25:15-08:00","id":46651,"title":"","content":"Personally I'm thinking that, in my games, the &quot;scales of the blood&quot;, which will allow for lighter feeding restrictions and to combat torpor, will be devotions based off of different coils, and perhaps even some scales. This I intend to use as the reason why such mastery is rare.<br /> Some parts of the curse are difficult to change, the need for blood and the call of torpor in particular, and some skill is needed in several different coils to have any chance of manipulating them.<br /> Of course the elders, and ancillae, that manage to learn such things are also given commensurate respect by their peers and enemies. After all, who wouldn't be a bit creeped out by the hundred year old who just doesn't seem to feed, ever? Is he even a vampire? He seems to be...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T15:36:14-07:00","id":183283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32998-b-s-coil-of-blood-souls?p=42987#post42987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Just a couple of things:<br /> I'm wondering, can a vampire with BP2+ spend more than 1 Vitae to activate Physical Intensity? If so, this could get kinda ridiculous. If not, this is pretty cool and definitely coil material.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>How about, instead of doubling the intensity, making it last 2 turns per expenditure? That would be a logical development from &quot;blood seeps slowly.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T17:45:01-07:00","id":1382271,"title":"","content":"To pendragon, I always just allowed &quot;the coil of the blood&quot; as just another coil, players could take. Not changing it a bit, I mean 2nd edition does say &quot;these aren't all the coils&quot; and people are encouraged to create their own. I just added the coils in ver. 1 to 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25914-alucardknight","name":"AlucardKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T17:48:47-07:00","id":1382272,"title":"","content":"Well with &quot;scales&quot; and given that the &quot;dragons&quot; are supposed to be arcane and &quot;mystical&quot; (never understood that one) I'd say the scales of the coil of the blood, allow one use abilities, kinda of the flavor of what the old VTM <b>Quietus</b> did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25914-alucardknight","name":"AlucardKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T18:47:48-07:00","id":1382276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AlucardKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32998-b-s-coil-of-blood-souls?p=1382271#post1382271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To pendragon, I always just allowed &quot;the coil of the blood&quot; as just another coil, players could take. Not changing it a bit, I mean 2nd edition does say &quot;these aren't all the coils&quot; and people are encouraged to create their own. I just added the coils in ver. 1 to 2.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The problem with just adding Coils from 1e is that you will lack 1-2 tiers (depending on which Coil and which books you have access to), are often unbalanced (sometimes even in first edition), often clashes with second edition design philosophies or themes, and might not even work properly if they interact with rules that has changed between editions.<br /> For example, Blood of Beasts (second dot of Coil of Blood) is 1.) wholly passive when 2e Coils are supposed to be interacted with as to make them more interesting and 2.) ridiculously good for its level considering how much of a problem feeding at BP6+ is supposed to be in second edition. Another example is Sun's Forgotten Kiss (third dot of Coil of Banes) that just straight up doesn't work in second edition because the rules for how vampires take damage from sunlight has changed (as well as being extremely underwhelming for what used to be the capstone dot for that Coil, even within the context of first edition).<br /> There are reasons why there have been so many attempts to update the 1e Coils to fit with VtR 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T21:04:46-07:00","id":1382282,"title":"","content":"Well I always hated the whole &quot;vampires need to feed on other vampires&quot;, that doesn't make them monsters, or scary for humans... It makes them a &quot;self-solving problem&quot;.. It's a part of the game I often abandon, so the second tier always made more sense to me. As for some of the other &quot;coils&quot; yeah, that is a problem in fact there is one coil that just allows vamps to fake eating food (which has become redundant), So of course it's a &quot;coil by coil&quot; kinda distinction, Them missing one level (yes I do have all the core books) isn't really that big a problem, you just boost some levels, like &quot;orphaned blood&quot; is now kinda in the vouivode coil, so it has to be lost and something else needs put there (I put that animal blood gives +1 to blood pool regardless of size, your consuming it's life, not precisely it's blood volume) Plus it makes it easier for players that want to &quot;explore&quot; areas, where there isn't necessarily humans around (you can only make so many &quot;coincidental campers&quot; before everyone rolls their eyes) <br /> <br /> The third for coil of banes? That one is a bit odd, but as for the rules, the coils are meant to change those, I mean fundamentally change the curse and what they are.. So I still let them apply it. but for the most part the &quot;coil of the ascendant&quot; makes it redundant. So in that, your right.. But if characters wanna blow xp on it, so be it. I think of the 2nd edition coils as something &quot;new&quot; found out by the order, a &quot;better way&quot; so to speak. (that's so the two ver. &quot;mesh&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25914-alucardknight","name":"AlucardKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T21:10:13-07:00","id":1382283,"title":"","content":"I've often liked the ad&amp;d version of vamps, in that setting, vampire blood is deadly to other vamps (kinda like &quot;dead-man's blood&quot; in supernatural) so the 5th tier of &quot;coil of blood&quot; makes the vampire's blood just that, Extremely deadly to drink unless willingly given (but only to other vampires)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25914-alucardknight","name":"AlucardKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T21:20:50-07:00","id":1382284,"title":"","content":"I always thought that the whole &quot;high levels of potency made vamps feed only from vamps&quot; was really silly, and it was very much an OBVIOUS game-mechanic, I mean really, it takes the edge off of &quot;they eat people&quot;, What's a vampire hunter got to fear? They don't &quot;taste right&quot;... LOL it's a rather large problem. The blood potency going up after time, that made sense, after all why would it matter if a 300 year old vampire woke up if he was as basically the same power level as a 2 year old one!!! Also the sheer logistics is problematic, how does one take &quot;life&quot; exclusively from another corpse?... Isn't that like eating someone's vomit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25914-alucardknight","name":"AlucardKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T21:36:06-07:00","id":1382286,"title":"","content":"To be honest I never figured out how exactly that whole &quot;high blood potency&quot; and preying on vampires really worked with the Lancea Sanctum... Isn't that kinda contrary to everything they believe? It really doesn't work anyway you look at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25914-alucardknight","name":"AlucardKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T21:44:10-07:00","id":1382287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AlucardKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32998-b-s-coil-of-blood-souls?p=1382284#post1382284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought that the whole &quot;high levels of potency made vamps feed only from vamps&quot; was really silly, and it was very much an OBVIOUS game-mechanic, I mean really, it takes the edge off of &quot;they eat people&quot;, What's a vampire hunter got to fear?</div> </div> </div> </div>That an old and powerful vampire starts wanting/having to <i>make more vampires</i>. It's an impetus for Kindred to form dynasties.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They don't &quot;taste right&quot;... LOL it's a rather large problem. The blood potency going up after time, that made sense, after all why would it matter if a 300 year old vampire woke up if he was as basically the same power level as a 2 year old one!!! </div> </div> </div>If Blood Potency was the only measure of a vampire's power then there would be no point in tracking experience. The old Primogen woke up and he's down to BP2? Whatever, man, the guy spent sixty straight years building up a portfolio of magic tricks and was personally responsible for half the weird architectural quirks in the city, you can unlive with the fact that he can drink from a bank teller without forcing it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also the sheer logistics is problematic, how does one take &quot;life&quot; exclusively from another corpse?... Isn't that like eating someone's vomit? </div> </div> </div>Vitae is gotten by vampires processing stolen life. It doesn't do anything in the vampire's system while it's not being expended aside from be a mystically potent and addictive bloodlike substance. Vampires aren't biologically alive, but they <i>are</i> unliving vessels of raw life-essence.<br /> <br /> What you feed on informs your general vibe as a vampire about as much as where you sleep, and feeding on other vampires means you're likely eating more of a blend than you used to be in addition to no longer being at risk for getting caught up in the rush of consuming refined hard cocaine. If your childer claim the three most popular night clubs as their hunting grounds and you use them to feed, you're King Shit when it comes to Vampires That Hunt In Popular Night Clubs even if you haven't set foot on a dance floor since the disco days.<br /> <br /> <br /> Unrelatedly, there is an Edit button that you would be better-served using instead of making <s>three</s> four posts in a row to express the same basic thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T05:23:07-07:00","id":1382319,"title":"","content":"Since this thread was started the Coil of Ziva has been made that combines Ladder and Locust together in a sense. Soul is sort of covered by Ascendant so all that\u2019s really missing is the ability to get by on less blood than everyone else and Half Damed offers a starting point for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}